            <ArticleTitle>Failure of selenium-ace to improve osteoarthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>211-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Selenium-ACE, a formulation containing the trace element selenium with three vitamins, is widely promoted for the treatment of arthritis. A controlled double-blind trial of Selenium-ACE in osteoarthritis failed to demonstrate any significant efficacy for the compound over placebo at 3 or 6 months though there was a non-significant trend to improvement in some clinical parameters in both groups. Side-effects were more frequently seen in the placebo group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
